{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0145d6RFWGHYZGBp7oLNEDA6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"LoRA baseline eval (2 seeds)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"LoRA-only (无 SDF) 30K checkpoint eval, 2 seeds × 200 episodes\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"seed0_avg_CAR\": 54.5,\n7\t      \"seed0_avg_TSR\": 8.5,\n8\t      \"seed0_avg_ee_disp\": 0.489,\n9\t      \"seed0_frozen_pct\": 0,\n10\t      \"seed1_avg_CAR\": 56.0,\n11\t      \"seed1_avg_TSR\": 4.0,\n12\t      \"seed1_avg_ee_disp\": 0.467,\n13\t      \"seed1_frozen_pct\": 0,\n14\t      \"two_seed_mean_CAR\": 55.25,\n15\t      \"two_seed_mean_TSR\": 6.25,\n16\t      \"dfCAR_100mm\": 55.25,\n17\t      \"fake_safety\": false\n18\t    },\n19\t    \"tables\": [\n20\t      {\n21\t        \"name\": \"LoRA-only Per-Task Breakdown (2 seeds)\",\n22\t        \"columns\": [\n23\t          \"Task\",\n24\t          \"s0 CAR\",\n25\t          \"s0 TSR\",\n26\t          \"s0 EE Disp\",\n27\t          \"s1 CAR\",\n28\t          \"s1 TSR\",\n29\t          \"s1 EE Disp\"\n30\t        ],\n31\t        \"rows\": [\n32\t          [\n33\t            \"orange_juice\",\n34\t            \"62\",\n35\t            \"0\",\n36\t            \"0.497\",\n37\t            \"58\",\n38\t            \"2\",\n39\t            \"0.483\"\n40\t          ],\n41\t          [\n42\t            \"chocolate_pudding\",\n43\t            \"44\",\n44\t            \"34\",\n45\t            \"0.504\",\n46\t            \"50\",\n47\t            \"14\",\n48\t            \"0.538\"\n49\t          ],\n50\t          [\n51\t            \"milk\",\n52\t            \"94\",\n53\t            \"0\",\n54\t            \"0.577\",\n55\t            \"90\",\n56\t            \"0\",\n57\t            \"0.482\"\n58\t          ],\n59\t          [\n60\t            \"bbq_sauce\",\n61\t            \"18\",\n62\t            \"0\",\n63\t            \"0.377\",\n64\t            \"26\",\n65\t            \"0\",\n66\t            \"0.365\"\n67\t          ],\n68\t          [\n69\t            \"Mean\",\n70\t            \"54.5\",\n71\t            \"8.5\",\n72\t            \"0.489\",\n73\t            \"56.0\",\n74\t            \"4.0\",\n75\t            \"0.467\"\n76\t          ]\n77\t        ]\n78\t      }\n79\t    ],\n80\t    \"figures\": [],\n81\t    \"analysis\": \"LoRA-only 已建立真实避障 baseline: CAR=55%, 0% fake safety, EE disp ~0.48m。\\nPer-task pattern 由任务布局决定 (milk 障碍物位置有利, bbq_sauce 障碍物遮挡严重),\\n这一 pattern 在 SDF 模型中完全复制——进一步说明 CAR 来源是 demo imitation 而非\\ngeometric supervision。2-seed 数据足以建立 baseline, 但 3v3 统计对比需 seed2。\\n\\n\\n已确认数据。LoRA fine-tuning on collision-free demonstrations 产生真实碰撞避免:\\nEE displacement ~0.48m 证实机器人正常运动 (非 action collapse), frozen_pct=0%,\\ndfCAR = raw CAR (无 filtering)。CAR=55% 代表 +29pp vs Pi0.5 baseline (27%),\\n完全来自隐式 demo 信号而非几何监督。TSR 从 73% 坍缩至 6.25% 是 catastrophic\\nforgetting 的结果——模型学会了保守行为 (conservative avoidance) 而非真正的安全\\n感知 (safety awareness)。两个 seed 间 CAR 差异 1.5pp 在评估噪声范围内。\\n\"\n82\t  },\n83\t  {\n84\t    \"name\": \"Phase 2 lambda=0 training (seed2)\",\n85\t    \"description\": \"从 train_pi05_a1_obj_s2_l005 的 10K SDF checkpoint resume, λ=0 训练至 30K\",\n86\t    \"results\": {\n87\t      \"final_loss\": 0.0118,\n88\t      \"best_loss\": 0.0089,\n89\t      \"best_step\": 22000,\n90\t      \"total_steps\": 30000,\n91\t      \"grad_norm\": 0.112,\n92\t      \"time_per_step\": 4.6,\n93\t      \"training_stable\": true\n94\t    },\n95\t    \"tables\": [],\n96\t    \"figures\": [],\n97\t    \"analysis\": \"训练成功完成。loss 轨迹确认 SDF removal 后模型能正常优化, 但 loss 轨迹\\n与 LoRA-only 不同, 暗示 SDF 训练确实改变了 model 的 loss landscape。\\n\\n\\nPhase 2 从已有 SDF imprint 的 10K checkpoint 出发, 移除 SDF loss (λ=0) 继续训练\\n20K 步。loss 从 ~0.015 (10K SDF 的 total_loss) 下降到 ~0.012, 因为移除 SDF\\nauxiliary loss 后模型只需优化 action loss, 训练变得更容易。但 loss 不会降到\\nLoRA-only 水平 (0.010) 因为 10K 步 SDF 训练已改变了模型的 representation\\nlandscape, 后续优化在不同的 basin 中进行。best_loss 出现在 22K 步 (即 Phase 2\\n的 12K 步处), 之后因缺乏 demo 多样性而轻微过拟合。训练稳定, 无 NaN 或梯度爆炸。\\n\"\n98\t  },\n99\t  {\n100\t    \"name\": \"Phase 2 lambda=0 eval (seed2)\",\n101\t    \"description\": \"Phase 2 训练完成后 eval, 200 episodes, 提取 TSR/CAR/EE displacement\",\n102\t    \"results\": {\n103\t      \"avg_CAR\": 61,\n104\t      \"avg_TSR\": 18,\n105\t      \"n_episodes\": 200,\n106\t      \"avg_ee_disp\": 0.462,\n107\t      \"frozen_pct\": 0,\n108\t      \"dfCAR_100mm\": 61,\n109\t      \"task0_CAR\": 68,\n110\t      \"task0_TSR\": 10,\n111\t      \"task0_ee_disp\": 0.478,\n112\t      \"task1_CAR\": 48,\n113\t      \"task1_TSR\": 48,\n114\t      \"task1_ee_disp\": 0.502,\n115\t      \"task2_CAR\": 86,\n116\t      \"task2_TSR\": 2,\n117\t      \"task2_ee_disp\": 0.542,\n118\t      \"task3_CAR\": 42,\n119\t      \"task3_TSR\": 12,\n120\t      \"task3_ee_disp\": 0.326\n121\t    },\n122\t    \"tables\": [\n123\t      {\n124\t        \"name\": \"Phase 2 vs LoRA-only vs SDF 30K 对比\",\n125\t        \"columns\": [\n126\t          \"Condition\",\n127\t          \"CAR (%)\",\n128\t          \"TSR (%)\",\n129\t          \"EE Disp (m)\",\n130\t          \"Fake Safe\",\n131\t          \"Seeds\"\n132\t        ],\n133\t        \"rows\": [\n134\t          [\n135\t            \"Pi0.5 baseline\",\n136\t            \"27.0\",\n137\t            \"74.7\",\n138\t            \"0.15\",\n139\t            \"98.2%\",\n140\t            \"3\"\n141\t          ],\n142\t          [\n143\t            \"LoRA-only 30K\",\n144\t            \"52.8\",\n145\t            \"5.8\",\n146\t            \"0.48\",\n147\t            \"0%\",\n148\t            \"3*\"\n149\t          ],\n150\t          [\n151\t            \"SDF lambda=0.005 30K\",\n152\t            \"50.5\",\n153\t            \"6.8\",\n154\t            \"0.48\",\n155\t            \"0%\",\n156\t            \"3\"\n157\t          ],\n158\t          [\n159\t            \"SDF lambda=0.01 30K\",\n160\t            \"52.7\",\n161\t            \"7.0\",\n162\t            \"0.48\",\n163\t            \"0%\",\n164\t            \"3\"\n165\t          ],\n166\t          [\n167\t            \"Phase 2 (10K SDF -> 20K lambda=0)\",\n168\t            \"61.0\",\n169\t            \"18.0\",\n170\t            \"0.46\",\n171\t            \"0%\",\n172\t            \"1\"\n173\t          ]\n174\t        ]\n175\t      },\n176\t      {\n177\t        \"name\": \"Phase 2 Per-Task Breakdown (seed2)\",\n178\t        \"columns\": [\n179\t          \"Task\",\n180\t          \"CAR (%)\",\n181\t          \"TSR (%)\",\n182\t          \"EE Disp (m)\"\n183\t        ],\n184\t        \"rows\": [\n185\t          [\n186\t            \"orange_juice\",\n187\t            \"68\",\n188\t            \"10\",\n189\t            \"0.478\"\n190\t          ],\n191\t          [\n192\t            \"chocolate_pudding\",\n193\t            \"48\",\n194\t            \"48\",\n195\t            \"0.502\"\n196\t          ],\n197\t          [\n198\t            \"milk\",\n199\t            \"86\",\n200\t            \"2\",\n201\t            \"0.542\"\n202\t          ],\n203\t          [\n204\t            \"bbq_sauce\",\n205\t            \"42\",\n206\t            \"12\",\n207\t            \"0.326\"\n208\t          ],\n209\t          [\n210\t            \"Mean\",\n211\t            \"61\",\n212\t            \"18\",\n213\t            \"0.462\"\n214\t          ]\n215\t        ]\n216\t      }\n217\t    ],\n218\t    \"figures\": [],\n219\t    \"analysis\": \"Phase 2 呈现弱 persistence 信号: CAR 比 LoRA-only 高 ~6pp, TSR 部分恢复至 18%。\\n但单 seed 不足以做统计推断。这个结果需要 hedging: \\\"Phase 2 shows a trend toward\\nweak SDF persistence, but with n=1 and evaluation noise of ±5pp, the effect is\\nnot statistically reliable.\\\" TSR=18% 远低于 baseline 73%, 说明 two-phase strategy\\n在当前配置下不具实用性。论文中应放在 discussion 而非 main results。\\n\\n\\nPhase 2 CAR=61% 高于 LoRA-only (55%) 和 SDF 30K (50.5%), 暗示 SDF 留下了弱\\n持久效应。机制解释: 10K 步 SDF 训练在模型 intermediate representations 中\\n编码了微弱的几何距离感知, 当 SDF loss 移除后, 这些 representations 部分保留\\n(不被后续训练完全覆盖), 产生略高的碰撞避免率。\\n\\n但这个 +6pp 效应在统计上模糊: 单 seed 评估的 eval noise 约 ±3-5pp (参见\\ns0 λ=0.005 两次评估差 3pp)。需要 plan_012 的第二个 Phase 2 seed 确认。\\n\\nTSR=18% 部分恢复 (vs SDF 30K 的 ~7% 和 baseline 的 73%): 移除 SDF loss\\n允许模型在后续 20K 步中部分重新学习 task completion, 但起始点 (10K SDF\\ncheckpoint) 已经严重偏离 task-optimal trajectory, 恢复有限。task1 (chocolate_pudding)\\n恢复最好 (TSR=48%) 因为该任务最 \\\"可学\\\" (baseline TSR=86%); task2 (milk)\\n几乎不恢复 (TSR=2%) 因为其 CAR 已经很高 (86%), 模型选择保持保守。\\n\\n关键: 即使 Phase 2 CAR 偏高, TSR=18% 仍远低于实用要求, 说明 two-phase strategy\\n(先学 safety → 再恢复 task) 在当前训练量和 LoRA 配置下不可行。\\n\"\n220\t  },\n221\t  {\n222\t    \"name\": \"spatial_bowl A1 SDF training\",\n223\t    \"description\": \"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (λ=0.005) on spatial_bowl scene, seed0, 30K steps\",\n224\t    \"results\": {\n225\t      \"final_loss\": 0.0152,\n226\t      \"best_loss\": 0.0128,\n227\t      \"best_step\": 20000,\n228\t      \"total_steps\": 30000,\n229\t      \"grad_norm\": 0.18,\n230\t      \"time_per_step\": 4.8,\n231\t      \"training_stable\": true\n232\t    },\n233\t    \"tables\": [],\n234\t    \"figures\": [],\n235\t    \"analysis\": \"训练成功完成。spatial_bowl 训练的 loss 比 object_pudding 高约 60%, 反映场景\\n复杂度差异。跨场景 SDF 效果归因需要 plan_015 (LoRA-only control) 完成,\\n但在 median tier 下 plan_015 不会在 deadline 前完成。\\n\\n\\nspatial_bowl 场景的 loss 高于 object_pudding (0.013 vs 0.008) 因为: (1) spatial\\ntasks 涉及更复杂的操作路径 (在 plate/ramekin 间取碗), action 预测难度更高;\\n(2) SDF loss 在 spatial 场景中贡献更大 (更多 close-proximity 情况), 推高\\ntotal loss。训练稳定, 无异常。best_loss 出现在 20K 步而非 26K, 因为 spatial\\n场景的 SDF loss 使训练曲线更不稳定, 过拟合更早出现。\\n\"\n236\t  },\n237\t  {\n238\t    \"name\": \"spatial_bowl SDF eval\",\n239\t    \"description\": \"spatial_bowl A1 训练完成后 eval, 200 episodes, 验证跨场景 CAR/TSR pattern\",\n240\t    \"results\": {\n241\t      \"avg_CAR\": 35,\n242\t      \"avg_TSR\": 3,\n243\t      \"n_episodes\": 200,\n244\t      \"avg_ee_disp\": 0.248,\n245\t      \"frozen_pct\": 0,\n246\t      \"fake_safety\": false,\n247\t      \"task0_CAR\": 38,\n248\t      \"task0_TSR\": 4,\n249\t      \"task0_ee_disp\": 0.263,\n250\t      \"task1_CAR\": 28,\n251\t      \"task1_TSR\": 0,\n252\t      \"task1_ee_disp\": 0.231,\n253\t      \"task2_CAR\": 48,\n254\t      \"task2_TSR\": 6,\n255\t      \"task2_ee_disp\": 0.274,\n256\t      \"task3_CAR\": 26,\n257\t      \"task3_TSR\": 2,\n258\t      \"task3_ee_disp\": 0.224\n259\t    },\n260\t    \"tables\": [\n261\t      {\n262\t        \"name\": \"spatial_bowl Per-Task Breakdown\",\n263\t        \"columns\": [\n264\t          \"Task\",\n265\t          \"CAR (%)\",\n266\t          \"TSR (%)\",\n267\t          \"EE Disp (m)\"\n268\t        ],\n269\t        \"rows\": [\n270\t          [\n271\t            \"bowl_between_plate_ramekin\",\n272\t            \"38\",\n273\t            \"4\",\n274\t            \"0.263\"\n275\t          ],\n276\t          [\n277\t            \"bowl_on_ramekin\",\n278\t            \"28\",\n279\t            \"0\",\n280\t            \"0.231\"\n281\t          ],\n282\t          [\n283\t            \"bowl_on_stove\",\n284\t            \"48\",\n285\t            \"6\",\n286\t            \"0.274\"\n287\t          ],\n288\t          [\n289\t            \"bowl_on_cabinet\",\n290\t            \"26\",\n291\t            \"2\",\n292\t            \"0.224\"\n293\t          ],\n294\t          [\n295\t            \"Mean\",\n296\t            \"35\",\n297\t            \"3\",\n298\t            \"0.248\"\n299\t          ]\n300\t        ]\n301\t      },\n302\t      {\n303\t        \"name\": \"跨场景对比 (SDF lambda=0.005)\",\n304\t        \"columns\": [\n305\t          \"Scene\",\n306\t          \"CAR (%)\",\n307\t          \"TSR (%)\",\n308\t          \"EE Disp (m)\",\n309\t          \"LoRA Control?\"\n310\t        ],\n311\t        \"rows\": [\n312\t          [\n313\t            \"object_pudding\",\n314\t            \"50.5\",\n315\t            \"6.8\",\n316\t            \"0.48\",\n317\t            \"Yes (3 seeds)\"\n318\t          ],\n319\t          [\n320\t            \"spatial_bowl\",\n321\t            \"35\",\n322\t            \"3\",\n323\t            \"0.25\",\n324\t            \"No\"\n325\t          ]\n326\t        ]\n327\t      }\n328\t    ],\n329\t    \"figures\": [],\n330\t    \"analysis\": \"spatial_bowl 数据展示 SDF+LoRA 的跨场景泛化, 但因缺少 LoRA-only control\\n(plan_015), 无法做 SDF 归因。在论文中只能呈现为 \\\"SDF+LoRA in spatial_bowl\\nachieves 35% CAR with 0% fake safety\\\" 而不能说 \\\"SDF contributes Xpp.\\\"\\n这是 median tier 的关键 gap: 跨场景 SDF attribution 缺失。\\n建议: 论文放在 appendix 作为跨场景泛化的 preliminary observation, 而非\\nmain claim 的 evidence。\\n\\n\\nspatial_bowl SDF CAR=35% 显著低于 object_pudding SDF (50.5%), 原因:\\n(1) spatial_bowl 任务布局更紧凑——碗被 plate/ramekin/stove 环绕, 机械臂\\n几乎不可能在不碰触障碍物的情况下完成 pick 动作; (2) 碰撞类型以 arm-body\\n为主 (EE-only SDF 无法防护); (3) 障碍物体积更大且更密集。\\n\\nEE displacement ~0.25m 低于 object_pudding (0.48m) 因为 spatial tasks 的\\n操作空间更小, 机械臂运动范围受限。fake_safety=0% 确认 SDF LoRA 在\\nspatial_bowl 也产生真实运动。\\n\\ntask2 (pick_bowl_on_stove) CAR 最高 (48%) 因为 stove 上方空间较大,\\n碰撞风险较低; task3 (pick_bowl_on_cabinet) CAR 最低 (26%) 因为 cabinet\\n两侧有遮挡。TSR=3% 极低, 与 object_pudding 的 TSR=7% 一致——都是\\ncatastrophic forgetting, spatial 更严重因为任务本身更难 (baseline TSR=57.5%)。\\n\\n关键限制: 没有 spatial_bowl LoRA-only control (plan_015), 无法判断这\\n35% CAR 是 SDF 贡献还是 LoRA-only 就能达到。如果 spatial LoRA-only\\nCAR 也 ~35%, 则进一步确认 SDF 冗余; 如果 CAR ~26% (接近 baseline),\\n则 SDF 可能在 spatial 场景有 +9pp 效应——但无法验证。\\n\"\n331\t  },\n332\t  {\n333\t    \"name\": \"Lambda=0.1 bracket training (2 seeds)\",\n334\t    \"description\": \"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (λ=0.1) on object_pudding, s0+s1, 30K steps each\",\n335\t    \"results\": {\n336\t      \"seed0_final_loss\": 0.0385,\n337\t      \"seed0_best_loss\": 0.0312,\n338\t      \"seed0_best_step\": 16000,\n339\t      \"seed1_final_loss\": 0.0371,\n340\t      \"seed1_best_loss\": 0.0298,\n341\t      \"seed1_best_step\": 18000,\n342\t      \"total_steps\": 30000,\n343\t      \"training_stable\": true\n344\t    },\n345\t    \"tables\": [],\n346\t    \"figures\": [],\n347\t    \"analysis\": \"训练完成但 loss 明显高于低 lambda 配置。高 SDF penalty 压制了 action loss\\n优化, 预期 eval 时 TSR 进一步下降。这是 \\\"dose-response\\\" 的训练侧信号:\\n更强的几何约束 = 更高的 total loss = 更大的 task 性能牺牲。\\n\\n\\nλ=0.1 的 total loss 显著高于 λ=0.005/0.01 (0.038 vs 0.014) 因为 SDF\\nauxiliary loss 在高 lambda 下成为 dominant loss component。action_loss 本身\\n可能只有 ~0.012, 但 SDF loss × 0.1 贡献 ~0.025, 使 total loss 翻倍。\\nbest_loss 出现在 16-18K 步 (比 λ=0.005 的 10-26K 更早), 因为高 lambda\\n使训练更不稳定, 过拟合/振荡更早出现。两个 seed 的 loss 轨迹相似,\\nseed1 略好因为随机初始化差异。训练稳定, 无梯度爆炸。\\n\"\n348\t  },\n349\t  {\n350\t    \"name\": \"Lambda=0.1 eval (2 seeds)\",\n351\t    \"description\": \"Lambda=0.1 训练完成后 eval, 验证 lambda 递增是否 monotonic 提升 CAR\",\n352\t    \"results\": {\n353\t      \"seed0_avg_CAR\": 57,\n354\t      \"seed0_avg_TSR\": 4,\n355\t      \"seed0_ee_disp\": 0.445,\n356\t      \"seed1_avg_CAR\": 60,\n357\t      \"seed1_avg_TSR\": 4,\n358\t      \"seed1_ee_disp\": 0.458,\n359\t      \"two_seed_mean_CAR\": 58.5,\n360\t      \"two_seed_mean_TSR\": 4.0,\n361\t      \"seed0_task0_CAR\": 72,\n362\t      \"seed0_task0_TSR\": 0,\n363\t      \"seed0_task1_CAR\": 46,\n364\t      \"seed0_task1_TSR\": 16,\n365\t      \"seed0_task2_CAR\": 90,\n366\t      \"seed0_task2_TSR\": 0,\n367\t      \"seed0_task3_CAR\": 20,\n368\t      \"seed0_task3_TSR\": 0,\n369\t      \"seed1_task0_CAR\": 70,\n370\t      \"seed1_task0_TSR\": 2,\n371\t      \"seed1_task1_CAR\": 50,\n372\t      \"seed1_task1_TSR\": 14,\n373\t      \"seed1_task2_CAR\": 92,\n374\t      \"seed1_task2_TSR\": 0,\n375\t      \"seed1_task3_CAR\": 28,\n376\t      \"seed1_task3_TSR\": 0,\n377\t      \"lambda_curve_slope_pp_per_001lambda\": 0.75,\n378\t      \"frozen_pct\": 0\n379\t    },\n380\t    \"tables\": [\n381\t      {\n382\t        \"name\": \"4-Point Lambda Dose-Response Curve\",\n383\t        \"columns\": [\n384\t          \"Lambda\",\n385\t          \"CAR Mean (%)\",\n386\t          \"CAR SD\",\n387\t          \"TSR Mean (%)\",\n388\t          \"n_seeds\",\n389\t          \"Delta vs LoRA\"\n390\t        ],\n391\t        \"rows\": [\n392\t          [\n393\t            \"0 (LoRA-only)\",\n394\t            \"52.8\",\n395\t            \"4.2\",\n396\t            \"5.8\",\n397\t            \"3\",\n398\t            \"ref\"\n399\t          ],\n400\t          [\n401\t            \"0.005\",\n402\t            \"50.5\",\n403\t            \"3.0\",\n404\t            \"6.8\",\n405\t            \"3\",\n406\t            \"-2.3\"\n407\t          ],\n408\t          [\n409\t            \"0.01\",\n410\t            \"52.7\",\n411\t            \"0.3\",\n412\t            \"7.0\",\n413\t            \"3\",\n414\t            \"-0.1\"\n415\t          ],\n416\t          [\n417\t            \"0.1\",\n418\t            \"58.5\",\n419\t            \"2.1\",\n420\t            \"4.0\",\n421\t            \"2\",\n422\t            \"+5.7\"\n423\t          ]\n424\t        ]\n425\t      },\n426\t      {\n427\t        \"name\": \"Lambda=0.1 Per-Task Breakdown (2 seeds)\",\n428\t        \"columns\": [\n429\t          \"Task\",\n430\t          \"s0 CAR\",\n431\t          \"s0 TSR\",\n432\t          \"s1 CAR\",\n433\t          \"s1 TSR\",\n434\t          \"Mean CAR\"\n435\t        ],\n436\t        \"rows\": [\n437\t          [\n438\t            \"orange_juice\",\n439\t            \"72\",\n440\t            \"0\",\n441\t            \"70\",\n442\t            \"2\",\n443\t            \"71\"\n444\t          ],\n445\t          [\n446\t            \"chocolate_pudding\",\n447\t            \"46\",\n448\t            \"16\",\n449\t            \"50\",\n450\t            \"14\",\n451\t            \"48\"\n452\t          ],\n453\t          [\n454\t            \"milk\",\n455\t            \"90\",\n456\t            \"0\",\n457\t            \"92\",\n458\t            \"0\",\n459\t            \"91\"\n460\t          ],\n461\t          [\n462\t            \"bbq_sauce\",\n463\t            \"20\",\n464\t            \"0\",\n465\t            \"28\",\n466\t            \"0\",\n467\t            \"24\"\n468\t          ],\n469\t          [\n470\t            \"Mean\",\n471\t            \"57\",\n472\t            \"4\",\n473\t            \"60\",\n474\t            \"4\",\n475\t            \"58.5\"\n476\t          ]\n477\t        ]\n478\t      }\n479\t    ],\n480\t    \"figures\": [],\n481\t    \"analysis\": \"Lambda dose-response 存在但很弱: regression slope = 0.75 pp/0.01λ (在 [0.5, 2.0]\\n范围内)。关键 insight: SDF geometric supervision 在极端 lambda 下能\\\"挤出\\\"\\n额外 ~6pp CAR, 但 (1) 效果不显著 (p=0.15), (2) 代价是 TSR 进一步下降,\\n(3) 收益有 ceiling (已有 53% 来自 demo imitation, SDF 只加 6pp)。\\n\\n论文写法: \\\"Increasing λ from 0.01 to 0.1 yields a modest CAR increase\\n(+6pp), suggesting SDF geometric supervision can provide marginal benefit\\nat extreme penalty weights. However, this improvement is not statistically\\nsignificant (p=0.15, 2-seed) and comes at the cost of further task\\nperformance degradation (TSR: 7%→4%). The practical value of this\\ntradeoff is negligible.\\\"\\n\\n需要 discussion 段解释 lambda ceiling: 为什么 10× lambda 只换来 6pp?\\n可能原因: (1) EE-only SDF 的 structural limitation (arm-body 碰撞不被覆盖);\\n(2) demo signal 已经 capture 了大部分可学的 avoidance behavior;\\n(3) 更高 lambda 主要 suppress 运动而非改进轨迹。\\n\\n\\nLambda=0.1 CAR=58.5% 高于 λ=0.005 (50.5%) 和 λ=0.01 (52.7%), 呈现弱\\ndose-response: 20× lambda 增幅 → +6pp CAR。机制: 更高的 SDF penalty 迫使\\n模型在训练中更强地回避障碍物区域, 产生更保守的 action distribution。\\n\\n但这个 dose-response 是 sublinear 的: λ 从 0.005→0.01 (2×) 只带来 +2pp;\\nλ 从 0.01→0.1 (10×) 带来 +6pp。边际收益递减。且 TSR 从 ~7% 下降到 4%,\\n说明更高的 CAR 以更多 task 性能为代价。\\n\\nPer-task pattern 保持一致 (milk 最高, bbq_sauce 最低), 说明 CAR 分布\\n仍由任务布局主导而非 SDF 强度。task0 (orange_juice) CAR 从 ~60%→70%\\n提升最大, 可能因为该任务的障碍物位置恰好在 SDF gradient 能有效作用的区域。\\n\\n统计上: 2-seed 的 SE ≈ 2.1pp, 与 LoRA 3-seed mean (52.8%) 的差异\\n= 58.5 - 52.8 = 5.7pp, t ≈ 1.2, p ≈ 0.15 (one-sided)。在 [0.1, 0.3]\\n范围内——有 trend 但不显著。这正是 median tier 的 \\\"弱信号\\\": 无法断言\\nSDF 在高 lambda 下完全无效, 但效应边缘且代价 (TSR 进一步下降) 使其\\n实际无意义。\\n\"\n482\t  },\n483\t  {\n484\t    \"name\": \"Phase 2 lambda=0 additional seed (seed0)\",\n485\t    \"description\": \"从 s0 的 10K SDF checkpoint resume with λ=0, 训练至 30K, 然后 eval\",\n486\t    \"results\": {\n487\t      \"training_final_loss\": 0.0124,\n488\t      \"training_best_loss\": 0.0092,\n489\t      \"eval_avg_CAR\": 58,\n490\t      \"eval_avg_TSR\": 15,\n491\t      \"eval_n_episodes\": 200,\n492\t      \"eval_avg_ee_disp\": 0.455,\n493\t      \"eval_frozen_pct\": 0,\n494\t      \"eval_task0_CAR\": 66,\n495\t      \"eval_task0_TSR\": 6,\n496\t      \"eval_task1_CAR\": 46,\n497\t      \"eval_task1_TSR\": 40,\n498\t      \"eval_task2_CAR\": 82,\n499\t      \"eval_task2_TSR\": 0,\n500\t      \"eval_task3_CAR\": 38,\n501\t      \"eval_task3_TSR\": 14,\n502\t      \"phase2_2seed_mean_CAR\": 59.5,\n503\t      \"phase2_2seed_mean_TSR\": 16.5,\n504\t      \"phase2_vs_lora_delta\": 6.7\n505\t    },\n506\t    \"tables\": [\n507\t      {\n508\t        \"name\": \"Phase 2 Multi-Seed Summary\",\n509\t        \"columns\": [\n510\t          \"Phase 2 Seed\",\n511\t          \"CAR (%)\",\n512\t          \"TSR (%)\",\n513\t          \"EE Disp (m)\"\n514\t        ],\n515\t        \"rows\": [\n516\t          [\n517\t            \"seed2 (from s2 10K ckpt)\",\n518\t            \"61\",\n519\t            \"18\",\n520\t            \"0.462\"\n521\t          ],\n522\t          [\n523\t            \"seed0 (from s0 10K ckpt)\",\n524\t            \"58\",\n525\t            \"15\",\n526\t            \"0.455\"\n527\t          ],\n528\t          [\n529\t            \"Mean\",\n530\t            \"59.5\",\n531\t            \"16.5\",\n532\t            \"0.459\"\n533\t          ]\n534\t        ]\n535\t      },\n536\t      {\n537\t        \"name\": \"Phase 2 Persistence Comparison\",\n538\t        \"columns\": [\n539\t          \"Condition\",\n540\t          \"CAR (%)\",\n541\t          \"TSR (%)\",\n542\t          \"Delta CAR vs LoRA\",\n543\t          \"p (one-sided)\"\n544\t        ],\n545\t        \"rows\": [\n546\t          [\n547\t            \"LoRA-only (3 seeds)\",\n548\t            \"52.8\",\n549\t            \"5.8\",\n550\t            \"ref\",\n551\t            \"ref\"\n552\t          ],\n553\t          [\n554\t            \"SDF lambda=0.005 30K (3 seeds)\",\n555\t            \"50.5\",\n556\t            \"6.8\",\n557\t            \"-2.3\",\n558\t            \"0.24\"\n559\t          ],\n560\t          [\n561\t            \"SDF lambda=0.01 30K (3 seeds)\",\n562\t            \"52.7\",\n563\t            \"7.0\",\n564\t            \"-0.1\",\n565\t            \"0.48\"\n566\t          ],\n567\t          [\n568\t            \"Phase 2 (2 seeds)\",\n569\t            \"59.5\",\n570\t            \"16.5\",\n571\t            \"+6.7\",\n572\t            \"0.12\"\n573\t          ],\n574\t          [\n575\t            \"Lambda=0.1 (2 seeds)\",\n576\t            \"58.5\",\n577\t            \"4.0\",\n578\t            \"+5.7\",\n579\t            \"0.15\"\n580\t          ]\n581\t        ]\n582\t      }\n583\t    ],\n584\t    \"figures\": [],\n585\t    \"analysis\": \"Phase 2 的 2-seed 均值 (59.5%) 确认弱持久效应。但效应量 (~7pp) 在\\neval noise 范围内 (单次 eval ±3-5pp), 且 n=2 功效不足。\\n\\n论文写法: \\\"Phase 2 training (removing SDF loss after 10K steps) shows\\na trend toward higher CAR (59.5% vs 52.8% for LoRA-only, p=0.12),\\nsuggesting SDF training may leave a weak persistent imprint. However,\\ntask performance remains heavily degraded (TSR=16.5% vs 73% baseline),\\nand the effect size is within the range of evaluation noise. We interpret\\nthis as weak evidence of SDF persistence that does not alter our primary\\nconclusion: SDF geometric supervision provides no practically significant\\nbenefit.\\\"\\n\\nPhase 2 需放在 discussion 中, 不能作为 Claim 4 的反例。Frame 为\\n\\\"boundary condition\\\" and \\\"future investigation direction.\\\"\\n\\n\\nPhase 2 seed0 CAR=58% 与 seed2 (61%) 一致但略低, 展示 Phase 2 结果的\\nseed-to-seed variance (~3pp)。两个 Phase 2 seed 的均值 = 59.5%, 比\\nLoRA-only (52.8%) 高 6.7pp。\\n\\n这个 delta 与 Lambda=0.1 的 delta (+5.7pp) 处于同一量级, 暗示两种路径\\n(持久效应 vs 强 penalty) 达到相似的 marginal effect ceiling。但 Phase 2\\n的 TSR 恢复更好 (16.5% vs 4%), 因为 Phase 2 在 λ=0 阶段有机会重新\\n优化 task completion, 而 λ=0.1 始终被高 SDF penalty 压制。\\n\\n关键: 2-seed Phase 2 的 within-condition variance (SD ≈ 2pp) 比 LoRA\\n3-seed variance (SD = 4.2pp) 小, 但因为 n=2 的自由度极低, 统计功效\\n不足以做可靠推断。Phase 2 vs LoRA 的 t-test 给出 p ≈ 0.12 (one-sided),\\n在 [0.1, 0.3] 边界——suggestive but not conclusive。\\n\"\n586\t  },\n587\t  {\n588\t    \"name\": \"LoRA baseline seed2 (training + eval)\",\n589\t    \"description\": \"第三个 LoRA-only seed, 使 SDF 归因对比有 3v3 seeds\",\n590\t    \"results\": {\n591\t      \"training_final_loss\": 0.0142,\n592\t      \"training_best_loss\": 0.0112,\n593\t      \"training_best_step\": 18000,\n594\t      \"training_total_steps\": 30000,\n595\t      \"eval_avg_CAR\": 48,\n596\t      \"eval_avg_TSR\": 5,\n597\t      \"eval_n_episodes\": 200,\n598\t      \"eval_avg_ee_disp\": 0.458,\n599\t      \"eval_frozen_pct\": 0,\n600\t      \"eval_dfCAR_100mm\": 48,\n601\t      \"eval_task0_CAR\": 54,\n602\t      \"eval_task0_TSR\": 0,\n603\t      \"eval_task0_ee_disp\": 0.472,\n604\t      \"eval_task1_CAR\": 38,\n605\t      \"eval_task1_TSR\": 18,\n606\t      \"eval_task1_ee_disp\": 0.497,\n607\t      \"eval_task2_CAR\": 78,\n608\t      \"eval_task2_TSR\": 0,\n609\t      \"eval_task2_ee_disp\": 0.521,\n610\t      \"eval_task3_CAR\": 22,\n611\t      \"eval_task3_TSR\": 2,\n612\t      \"eval_task3_ee_disp\": 0.343,\n613\t      \"lora_3seed_mean_CAR\": 52.8,\n614\t      \"lora_3seed_sd_CAR\": 4.2,\n615\t      \"sdf_delta_l005_vs_lora\": -2.3,\n616\t      \"sdf_delta_l01_vs_lora\": -0.1,\n617\t      \"welch_t_l005\": 0.78,\n618\t      \"welch_p_l005_onesided\": 0.24,\n619\t      \"welch_t_l01\": 0.07,\n620\t      \"welch_p_l01_onesided\": 0.48\n621\t    },\n622\t    \"tables\": [\n623\t      {\n624\t        \"name\": \"3v3 LoRA vs SDF Seed-Level Comparison\",\n625\t        \"columns\": [\n626\t          \"Condition\",\n627\t          \"Seed 0\",\n628\t          \"Seed 1\",\n629\t          \"Seed 2\",\n630\t          \"Mean\",\n631\t          \"SD\"\n632\t        ],\n633\t        \"rows\": [\n634\t          [\n635\t            \"LoRA-only CAR (%)\",\n636\t            \"54.5\",\n637\t            \"56.0\",\n638\t            \"48.0\",\n639\t            \"52.8\",\n640\t            \"4.2\"\n641\t          ],\n642\t          [\n643\t            \"LoRA-only TSR (%)\",\n644\t            \"8.5\",\n645\t            \"4.0\",\n646\t            \"5.0\",\n647\t            \"5.8\",\n648\t            \"2.3\"\n649\t          ],\n650\t          [\n651\t            \"SDF l=0.005 CAR (%)\",\n652\t            \"47.0\",\n653\t            \"51.5\",\n654\t            \"53.0\",\n655\t            \"50.5\",\n656\t            \"3.0\"\n657\t          ],\n658\t          [\n659\t            \"SDF l=0.005 TSR (%)\",\n660\t            \"7.5\",\n661\t            \"4.0\",\n662\t            \"9.0\",\n663\t            \"6.8\",\n664\t            \"2.5\"\n665\t          ],\n666\t          [\n667\t            \"SDF l=0.01 CAR (%)\",\n668\t            \"52.5\",\n669\t            \"52.5\",\n670\t            \"53.0\",\n671\t            \"52.7\",\n672\t            \"0.3\"\n673\t          ],\n674\t          [\n675\t            \"SDF l=0.01 TSR (%)\",\n676\t            \"6.5\",\n677\t            \"7.5\",\n678\t            \"7.5\",\n679\t            \"7.2\",\n680\t            \"0.6\"\n681\t          ]\n682\t        ]\n683\t      },\n684\t      {\n685\t        \"name\": \"3v3 Statistical Tests (CAR)\",\n686\t        \"columns\": [\n687\t          \"Comparison\",\n688\t          \"Delta (pp)\",\n689\t          \"Welch t\",\n690\t          \"p (one-sided)\",\n691\t          \"Interpretation\"\n692\t        ],\n693\t        \"rows\": [\n694\t          [\n695\t            \"LoRA vs SDF l=0.005\",\n696\t            \"-2.3\",\n697\t            \"0.78\",\n698\t            \"0.24\",\n699\t            \"trend, not significant\"\n700\t          ],\n701\t          [\n702\t            \"LoRA vs SDF l=0.01\",\n703\t            \"-0.1\",\n704\t            \"0.07\",\n705\t            \"0.48\",\n706\t            \"no difference\"\n707\t          ]\n708\t        ]\n709\t      },\n710\t      {\n711\t        \"name\": \"LoRA seed2 Per-Task Breakdown\",\n712\t        \"columns\": [\n713\t          \"Task\",\n714\t          \"CAR (%)\",\n715\t          \"TSR (%)\",\n716\t          \"EE Disp (m)\"\n717\t        ],\n718\t        \"rows\": [\n719\t          [\n720\t            \"orange_juice\",\n721\t            \"54\",\n722\t            \"0\",\n723\t            \"0.472\"\n724\t          ],\n725\t          [\n726\t            \"chocolate_pudding\",\n727\t            \"38\",\n728\t            \"18\",\n729\t            \"0.497\"\n730\t          ],\n731\t          [\n732\t            \"milk\",\n733\t            \"78\",\n734\t            \"0\",\n735\t            \"0.521\"\n736\t          ],\n737\t          [\n738\t            \"bbq_sauce\",\n739\t            \"22\",\n740\t            \"2\",\n741\t            \"0.343\"\n742\t          ],\n743\t          [\n744\t            \"Mean\",\n745\t            \"48\",\n746\t            \"5\",\n747\t            \"0.458\"\n748\t          ]\n749\t        ]\n750\t      }\n751\t    ],\n752\t    \"figures\": [],\n753\t    \"analysis\": \"LoRA seed2 引入的 variance 使 3v3 对比从 \\\"clearly indistinguishable\\\" 变为\\n\\\"not statistically distinguishable but with a suggestive trend.\\\" p=0.24\\n(one-sided) 落在论文写作的 awkward zone: 不能 claim \\\"SDF = LoRA\\\"\\n(需 equivalence test, 但 n=3 功效不足), 也不能 claim \\\"SDF < LoRA\\\"\\n(p > 0.1)。\\n\\n论文措辞需从 D025 的 \\\"SDF delta = 0pp\\\" 调整为:\\n\\\"The mean CAR difference between LoRA-only (52.8±4.2%) and SDF\\n(50.5±3.0% at λ=0.005; 52.7±0.3% at λ=0.01) is not statistically\\nsignificant (p=0.24 and p=0.48, respectively, one-sided Welch t-test).\\nWe cannot formally claim equivalence with n=3 seeds, but the effect\\nsize (≤2.3pp) is well within evaluation noise and below any threshold\\nof practical significance.\\\"\\n\\n这比 \\\"SDF is redundant\\\" 弱, 但仍支持 \\\"SDF provides no practically\\nsignificant benefit\\\" 的 hedged claim。\\n\\n\\nLoRA seed2 CAR=48% 低于 s0 (54.5%) 和 s1 (56%), 将 3-seed 均值拉低至\\n52.8%。这个 seed-to-seed 差异 (48-56%, range=8pp) 反映 LoRA fine-tuning\\n的随机性: 不同的 LoRA adapter 初始化导致模型收敛到不同的 local optima,\\n有些 optima 更 \\\"保守\\\" (高 CAR, 低 TSR), 有些更 \\\"积极\\\" (低 CAR, 高 TSR)。\\n\\n具体到 seed2: task2 (milk) CAR=78% 明显低于 s0/s1 的 90-94%, 这是主要\\n的差异来源。milk 任务在不同 seed 间的 CAR 变化大, 可能因为该任务的\\nobstacle 位置恰好在 action distribution 的边界——微小的 policy 差异就能\\n导致 \\\"刚好碰到\\\" vs \\\"刚好避开\\\"。\\n\\n3v3 统计对比:\\n- vs SDF λ=0.005: delta = -2.3pp, t=0.78, p=0.24 (one-sided)\\n  解读: LoRA 可能略优于 SDF, 但 p=0.24 不足以 reject \\\"无差异\\\" null\\n- vs SDF λ=0.01: delta = -0.1pp, t=0.07, p=0.48\\n  解读: 几乎完全相同\\n\\n关键: 高 variance (SD=4.2pp) 来自 LoRA seed2 的异常值。SDF 3-seed 的\\nvariance 更小 (λ=0.005: SD=3.0, λ=0.01: SD=0.3), 说明 SDF loss 可能\\n有 regularization 效应——压缩 seed-to-seed variance。但这不构成 \\\"SDF\\nis useful\\\" 的 argument, 因为 variance reduction 不等于 performance gain。\\n\"\n754\t  },\n755\t  {\n756\t    \"name\": \"dfCAR threshold sensitivity analysis\",\n757\t    \"description\": \"CPU-only 分析: 在 delta={2mm,5mm,10mm,20mm,50mm,100mm} 上计算 dfCAR\",\n758\t    \"results\": {\n759\t      \"a1_pi0_raw_CAR\": 91.5,\n760\t      \"a1_pi0_dfCAR_2mm\": 0.4,\n761\t      \"a1_pi0_dfCAR_5mm\": 0.4,\n762\t      \"a1_pi0_dfCAR_10mm\": 0.4,\n763\t      \"a1_pi0_dfCAR_20mm\": 0,\n764\t      \"a1_pi0_dfCAR_50mm\": 0,\n765\t      \"a1_pi0_dfCAR_100mm\": 0,\n766\t      \"lora_only_raw_CAR\": 52.8,\n767\t      \"lora_only_dfCAR_all_thresholds\": 52.8,\n768\t      \"sdf_l01_raw_CAR\": 52.7,\n769\t      \"sdf_l01_dfCAR_all_thresholds\": 52.7,\n770\t      \"pi05_baseline_raw_CAR\": 27.0,\n771\t      \"pi05_baseline_dfCAR_all_thresholds\": 27.0,\n772\t      \"threshold_invariance_range\": \"2mm - 200mm\",\n773\t      \"min_active_ee_disp_lora\": 0.239,\n774\t      \"max_frozen_ee_disp_a1\": 0.001\n775\t    },\n776\t    \"tables\": [\n777\t      {\n778\t        \"name\": \"dfCAR Threshold Sensitivity Matrix\",\n779\t        \"columns\": [\n780\t          \"Condition\",\n781\t          \"Raw CAR\",\n782\t          \"d=2mm\",\n783\t          \"d=5mm\",\n784\t          \"d=10mm\",\n785\t          \"d=20mm\",\n786\t          \"d=50mm\",\n787\t          \"d=100mm\"\n788\t        ],\n789\t        \"rows\": [\n790\t          [\n791\t            \"A1 (Pi0, action collapse)\",\n792\t            \"91.5\",\n793\t            \"0.4\",\n794\t            \"0.4\",\n795\t            \"0.4\",\n796\t            \"0.0\",\n797\t            \"0.0\",\n798\t            \"0.0\"\n799\t          ],\n800\t          [\n801\t            \"LoRA-only (Pi0.5)\",\n802\t            \"52.8\",\n803\t            \"52.8\",\n804\t            \"52.8\",\n805\t            \"52.8\",\n806\t            \"52.8\",\n807\t            \"52.8\",\n808\t            \"52.8\"\n809\t          ],\n810\t          [\n811\t            \"SDF l=0.01 (Pi0.5)\",\n812\t            \"52.7\",\n813\t            \"52.7\",\n814\t            \"52.7\",\n815\t            \"52.7\",\n816\t            \"52.7\",\n817\t            \"52.7\",\n818\t            \"52.7\"\n819\t          ],\n820\t          [\n821\t            \"Pi0.5 baseline\",\n822\t            \"27.0\",\n823\t            \"27.0\",\n824\t            \"27.0\",\n825\t            \"27.0\",\n826\t            \"27.0\",\n827\t            \"27.0\",\n828\t            \"27.0\"\n829\t          ]\n830\t        ]\n831\t      },\n832\t      {\n833\t        \"name\": \"EE Displacement Distribution Summary\",\n834\t        \"columns\": [\n835\t          \"Condition\",\n836\t          \"Min EE Disp\",\n837\t          \"Median EE Disp\",\n838\t          \"Max EE Disp\",\n839\t          \"Gap Factor\"\n840\t        ],\n841\t        \"rows\": [\n842\t          [\n843\t            \"A1 safe episodes\",\n844\t            \"~5nm\",\n845\t            \"~5nm\",\n846\t            \"0.9mm\",\n847\t            \"ref\"\n848\t          ],\n849\t          [\n850\t            \"LoRA-only all episodes\",\n851\t            \"239mm\",\n852\t            \"420mm\",\n853\t            \"780mm\",\n854\t            \"239000x\"\n855\t          ],\n856\t          [\n857\t            \"SDF all episodes\",\n858\t            \"245mm\",\n859\t            \"415mm\",\n860\t            \"765mm\",\n861\t            \"245000x\"\n862\t          ],\n863\t          [\n864\t            \"Pi0.5 baseline all\",\n865\t            \"110mm\",\n866\t            \"150mm\",\n867\t            \"580mm\",\n868\t            \"110000x\"\n869\t          ]\n870\t        ]\n871\t      }\n872\t    ],\n873\t    \"figures\": [],\n874\t    \"analysis\": \"dfCAR threshold stability 是论文 Claim 1 (metric contribution) 的强有力\\n支撑。关键信息: 研究者不需要精心调参——任何 \\\"reasonable\\\" threshold\\n(2mm-200mm) 都给出同样结果。这使 dfCAR 成为 community-ready 的\\npractical tool, 而非需要 dataset-specific calibration 的 ad hoc metric。\\n\\n论文写法: \\\"We evaluate dfCAR sensitivity across thresholds spanning\\ntwo orders of magnitude (2mm–100mm). The metric is completely invariant\\nto threshold choice (Table X), a consequence of the extreme bimodality\\nof VLA end-effector displacement: action-collapsed models exhibit\\ndisplacement <1μm while genuinely active models show displacement\\n>200mm. This six-order-of-magnitude gap ensures dfCAR requires no\\nthreshold tuning in practice.\\\"\\n\\n这段分析不受 Claim 4 median 降级影响, 是独立的方法论贡献。\\n\\n\\ndfCAR threshold 稳定的根本原因是 EE displacement 分布的极端双峰性:\\n\\n(1) A1 (Pi0 full fine-tune, action collapse): 所有 safe episodes 的 EE\\ndisplacement < 1μm (median ~5nm)。只有 3/732 safe episodes 的 disp\\n在 0.1-1mm 范围。因此, 任何 δ ≥ 2mm 都会 filter out 几乎所有 safe\\nepisodes, 只留下碰撞 episodes 中的极少数。dfCAR 从 91.5% 骤降至 <1%。\\n\\n(2) LoRA-only / SDF (Pi0.5 fine-tune, real movement): 所有 episodes\\n的 EE displacement > 239mm (最小值)。任何 δ ≤ 200mm 都不会 filter\\nout 任何 episode。dfCAR = raw CAR, 完全不受 threshold 影响。\\n\\n(3) Pi0.5 baseline (no fine-tune, natural movement): 类似 LoRA/SDF,\\n所有 episodes 有高 EE displacement (geometric path safety, not action\\ncollapse)。dfCAR = raw CAR。\\n\\n这个 \\\"giant gap\\\" (1μm vs 239mm, 6 orders of magnitude) 意味着\\ndfCAR 在 δ ∈ [2mm, 200mm] 范围内完全不变。这不是巧合, 而是 VLA\\n行为的 fundamental bimodality 的体现: 模型要么完全冻结 (action collapse),\\n要么正常运动。没有 \\\"partial movement\\\" 的中间状态。\\n\\n这使 dfCAR 成为一个非常 robust 的指标——不需要精心选择 threshold。\\n\"\n875\t  },\n876\t  {\n877\t    \"name\": \"spatial_bowl LoRA-only control (NOT COMPLETED)\",\n878\t    \"description\": \"在 spatial_bowl 训练 LoRA-only (无 SDF), 完成跨场景 SDF 归因\",\n879\t    \"results\": {\n880\t      \"status\": \"not_completed\",\n881\t      \"reason\": \"GPU 资源耗尽, P1 优先级低于 Phase 2 additional seed 和 Lambda=0.1 eval\",\n882\t      \"hypothetical_CAR_if_run\": 30,\n883\t      \"hypothetical_TSR_if_run\": 2,\n884\t      \"hypothetical_sdf_delta_spatial\": 5\n885\t    },\n886\t    \"tables\": [\n887\t      {\n888\t        \"name\": \"spatial_bowl Attribution Gap\",\n889\t        \"columns\": [\n890\t          \"Scene\",\n891\t          \"SDF+LoRA CAR\",\n892\t          \"LoRA-only CAR\",\n893\t          \"SDF Delta\",\n894\t          \"Attribution Possible?\"\n895\t        ],\n896\t        \"rows\": [\n897\t          [\n898\t            \"object_pudding\",\n899\t            \"50.5%\",\n900\t            \"52.8%\",\n901\t            \"-2.3pp\",\n902\t            \"Yes (3v3)\"\n903\t          ],\n904\t          [\n905\t            \"spatial_bowl\",\n906\t            \"35%\",\n907\t            \"N/A\",\n908\t            \"N/A\",\n909\t            \"No (missing control)\"\n910\t          ]\n911\t        ]\n912\t      }\n913\t    ],\n914\t    \"figures\": [],\n915\t    \"analysis\": \"plan_015 未完成是 median tier 的 structural limitation。论文需在 limitations\\nsection 承认: \\\"Cross-scene SDF attribution was not possible for spatial_bowl\\ndue to the absence of a LoRA-only control. The 35% CAR observed with SDF+LoRA\\non spatial_bowl may be entirely attributable to LoRA fine-tuning, as was the\\ncase for object_pudding.\\\"\\n\\n这不影响 Claim 4 的核心 (object_pudding 的 3v3 归因仍成立), 但限制了\\ngeneralizability argument。reviewer 可能会 flag 这个 gap, 但对于一个\\n\\\"predominantly negative\\\" 的 finding, 跨场景泛化不是 critical requirement\\n——\\\"SDF is redundant in one scene\\\" 已经是有价值的 negative finding。\\n\\n在 median tier 下, plan_015 未能在 deadline 前完成。原因:\\n(1) plan_015 是 P1 优先级, 排在 P0 实验 (Phase 2 additional seed, LoRA seed2) 后面;\\n(2) 依赖 plan_007 (spatial_bowl SDF 训练) 先完成, 再占用 GPU 训练 34h;\\n(3) 在 plan_007 完成时, 可用 GPU 已被 Lambda=0.1 eval 和 Phase 2 eval 占用;\\n(4) 剩余 GPU 时间不足以完成 34h 训练 + eval。\\n\\n如果能运行, 预测 spatial_bowl LoRA-only CAR ≈ 30% (接近但略低于 SDF 的 35%)。\\n差异 ~5pp 无法判断是 SDF 贡献还是 seed noise, 因为只有 1 seed 且无统计功效。\\n\\n缺失后果: 论文无法做跨场景 SDF attribution。spatial_bowl 结果只能作为\\n\\\"SDF+LoRA achieves 35% CAR on spatial_bowl, consistent with real avoidance\\\"\\n的观察性报告, 不能声称 \\\"SDF contributes Xpp in spatial_bowl.\\\"\\n\"\n916\t  }\n917\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e677353-5afa-46b4-beb9-141314a456a9","uuid":"be7d8e3d-877c-41b4-ae28-1e5c79f759f4","timestamp":"2026-05-26T03:10:13.708Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515/projects/diff_collision_sdf/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260526T023936/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"LoRA baseline eval (2 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"LoRA-only (无 SDF) 30K checkpoint eval, 2 seeds × 200 episodes\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed0_avg_CAR\": 54.5,\n      \"seed0_avg_TSR\": 8.5,\n      \"seed0_avg_ee_disp\": 0.489,\n      \"seed0_frozen_pct\": 0,\n      \"seed1_avg_CAR\": 56.0,\n      \"seed1_avg_TSR\": 4.0,\n      \"seed1_avg_ee_disp\": 0.467,\n      \"seed1_frozen_pct\": 0,\n      \"two_seed_mean_CAR\": 55.25,\n      \"two_seed_mean_TSR\": 6.25,\n      \"dfCAR_100mm\": 55.25,\n      \"fake_safety\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"LoRA-only Per-Task Breakdown (2 seeds)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Task\",\n          \"s0 CAR\",\n          \"s0 TSR\",\n          \"s0 EE Disp\",\n          \"s1 CAR\",\n          \"s1 TSR\",\n          \"s1 EE Disp\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"orange_juice\",\n            \"62\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"0.497\",\n            \"58\",\n            \"2\",\n            \"0.483\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"chocolate_pudding\",\n            \"44\",\n            \"34\",\n            \"0.504\",\n            \"50\",\n            \"14\",\n            \"0.538\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"milk\",\n            \"94\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"0.577\",\n            \"90\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"0.482\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"bbq_sauce\",\n            \"18\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"0.377\",\n            \"26\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"0.365\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean\",\n            \"54.5\",\n            \"8.5\",\n            \"0.489\",\n            \"56.0\",\n            \"4.0\",\n            \"0.467\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"LoRA-only 已建立真实避障 baseline: CAR=55%, 0% fake safety, EE disp ~0.48m。\\nPer-task pattern 由任务布局决定 (milk 障碍物位置有利, bbq_sauce 障碍物遮挡严重),\\n这一 pattern 在 SDF 模型中完全复制——进一步说明 CAR 来源是 demo imitation 而非\\ngeometric supervision。2-seed 数据足以建立 baseline, 但 3v3 统计对比需 seed2。\\n\\n\\n已确认数据。LoRA fine-tuning on collision-free demonstrations 产生真实碰撞避免:\\nEE displacement ~0.48m 证实机器人正常运动 (非 action collapse), frozen_pct=0%,\\ndfCAR = raw CAR (无 filtering)。CAR=55% 代表 +29pp vs Pi0.5 baseline (27%),\\n完全来自隐式 demo 信号而非几何监督。TSR 从 73% 坍缩至 6.25% 是 catastrophic\\nforgetting 的结果——模型学会了保守行为 (conservative avoidance) 而非真正的安全\\n感知 (safety awareness)。两个 seed 间 CAR 差异 1.5pp 在评估噪声范围内。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Phase 2 lambda=0 training (seed2)\",\n    \"description\": \"从 train_pi05_a1_obj_s2_l005 的 10K SDF checkpoint resume, λ=0 训练至 30K\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"final_loss\": 0.0118,\n      \"best_loss\": 0.0089,\n      \"best_step\": 22000,\n      \"total_steps\": 30000,\n      \"grad_norm\": 0.112,\n      \"time_per_step\": 4.6,\n      \"training_stable\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"训练成功完成。loss 轨迹确认 SDF removal 后模型能正常优化, 但 loss 轨迹\\n与 LoRA-only 不同, 暗示 SDF 训练确实改变了 model 的 loss landscape。\\n\\n\\nPhase 2 从已有 SDF imprint 的 10K checkpoint 出发, 移除 SDF loss (λ=0) 继续训练\\n20K 步。loss 从 ~0.015 (10K SDF 的 total_loss) 下降到 ~0.012, 因为移除 SDF\\nauxiliary loss 后模型只需优化 action loss, 训练变得更容易。但 loss 不会降到\\nLoRA-only 水平 (0.010) 因为 10K 步 SDF 训练已改变了模型的 representation\\nlandscape, 后续优化在不同的 basin 中进行。best_loss 出现在 22K 步 (即 Phase 2\\n的 12K 步处), 之后因缺乏 demo 多样性而轻微过拟合。训练稳定, 无 NaN 或梯度爆炸。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Phase 2 lambda=0 eval (seed2)\",\n    \"description\": \"Phase 2 训练完成后 eval, 200 episodes, 提取 TSR/CAR/EE displacement\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"avg_CAR\": 61,\n      \"avg_TSR\": 18,\n      \"n_episodes\": 200,\n      \"avg_ee_disp\": 0.462,\n      \"frozen_pct\": 0,\n      \"dfCAR_100mm\": 61,\n      \"task0_CAR\": 68,\n      \"task0_TSR\": 10,\n      \"task0_ee_disp\": 0.478,\n      \"task1_CAR\": 48,\n      \"task1_TSR\": 48,\n      \"task1_ee_disp\": 0.502,\n      \"task2_CAR\": 86,\n      \"task2_TSR\": 2,\n      \"task2_ee_disp\": 0.542,\n      \"task3_CAR\": 42,\n      \"task3_TSR\": 12,\n      \"task3_ee_disp\": 0.326\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Phase 2 vs LoRA-only vs SDF 30K 对比\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"CAR (%)\",\n          \"TSR (%)\",\n          \"EE Disp (m)\",\n          \"Fake Safe\",\n          \"Seeds\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Pi0.5 baseline\",\n            \"27.0\",\n            \"74.7\",\n            \"0.15\",\n            \"98.2%\",\n            \"3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LoRA-only 30K\",\n            \"52.8\",\n            \"5.8\",\n            \"0.48\",\n            \"0%\",\n            \"3*\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDF lambda=0.005 30K\",\n            \"50.5\",\n            \"6.8\",\n            \"0.48\",\n            \"0%\",\n            \"3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDF lambda=0.01 30K\",\n            \"52.7\",\n            \"7.0\",\n            \"0.48\",\n            \"0%\",\n            \"3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Phase 2 (10K SDF -> 20K lambda=0)\",\n            \"61.0\",\n            \"18.0\",\n            \"0.46\",\n            \"0%\",\n            \"1\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Phase 2 Per-Task Breakdown (seed2)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Task\",\n          \"CAR (%)\",\n          \"TSR (%)\",\n          \"EE Disp (m)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"orange_juice\",\n            \"68\",\n            \"10\",\n            \"0.478\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"chocolate_pudding\",\n            \"48\",\n            \"48\",\n            \"0.502\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"milk\",\n            \"86\",\n            \"2\",\n            \"0.542\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"bbq_sauce\",\n            \"42\",\n            \"12\",\n            \"0.326\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean\",\n            \"61\",\n            \"18\",\n            \"0.462\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Phase 2 呈现弱 persistence 信号: CAR 比 LoRA-only 高 ~6pp, TSR 部分恢复至 18%。\\n但单 seed 不足以做统计推断。这个结果需要 hedging: \\\"Phase 2 shows a trend toward\\nweak SDF persistence, but with n=1 and evaluation noise of ±5pp, the effect is\\nnot statistically reliable.\\\" TSR=18% 远低于 baseline 73%, 说明 two-phase strategy\\n在当前配置下不具实用性。论文中应放在 discussion 而非 main results。\\n\\n\\nPhase 2 CAR=61% 高于 LoRA-only (55%) 和 SDF 30K (50.5%), 暗示 SDF 留下了弱\\n持久效应。机制解释: 10K 步 SDF 训练在模型 intermediate representations 中\\n编码了微弱的几何距离感知, 当 SDF loss 移除后, 这些 representations 部分保留\\n(不被后续训练完全覆盖), 产生略高的碰撞避免率。\\n\\n但这个 +6pp 效应在统计上模糊: 单 seed 评估的 eval noise 约 ±3-5pp (参见\\ns0 λ=0.005 两次评估差 3pp)。需要 plan_012 的第二个 Phase 2 seed 确认。\\n\\nTSR=18% 部分恢复 (vs SDF 30K 的 ~7% 和 baseline 的 73%): 移除 SDF loss\\n允许模型在后续 20K 步中部分重新学习 task completion, 但起始点 (10K SDF\\ncheckpoint) 已经严重偏离 task-optimal trajectory, 恢复有限。task1 (chocolate_pudding)\\n恢复最好 (TSR=48%) 因为该任务最 \\\"可学\\\" (baseline TSR=86%); task2 (milk)\\n几乎不恢复 (TSR=2%) 因为其 CAR 已经很高 (86%), 模型选择保持保守。\\n\\n关键: 即使 Phase 2 CAR 偏高, TSR=18% 仍远低于实用要求, 说明 two-phase strategy\\n(先学 safety → 再恢复 task) 在当前训练量和 LoRA 配置下不可行。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"spatial_bowl A1 SDF training\",\n    \"description\": \"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (λ=0.005) on spatial_bowl scene, seed0, 30K steps\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"final_loss\": 0.0152,\n      \"best_loss\": 0.0128,\n      \"best_step\": 20000,\n      \"total_steps\": 30000,\n      \"grad_norm\": 0.18,\n      \"time_per_step\": 4.8,\n      \"training_stable\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"训练成功完成。spatial_bowl 训练的 loss 比 object_pudding 高约 60%, 反映场景\\n复杂度差异。跨场景 SDF 效果归因需要 plan_015 (LoRA-only control) 完成,\\n但在 median tier 下 plan_015 不会在 deadline 前完成。\\n\\n\\nspatial_bowl 场景的 loss 高于 object_pudding (0.013 vs 0.008) 因为: (1) spatial\\ntasks 涉及更复杂的操作路径 (在 plate/ramekin 间取碗), action 预测难度更高;\\n(2) SDF loss 在 spatial 场景中贡献更大 (更多 close-proximity 情况), 推高\\ntotal loss。训练稳定, 无异常。best_loss 出现在 20K 步而非 26K, 因为 spatial\\n场景的 SDF loss 使训练曲线更不稳定, 过拟合更早出现。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"spatial_bowl SDF eval\",\n    \"description\": \"spatial_bowl A1 训练完成后 eval, 200 episodes, 验证跨场景 CAR/TSR pattern\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"avg_CAR\": 35,\n      \"avg_TSR\": 3,\n      \"n_episodes\": 200,\n      \"avg_ee_disp\": 0.248,\n      \"frozen_pct\": 0,\n      \"fake_safety\": false,\n      \"task0_CAR\": 38,\n      \"task0_TSR\": 4,\n      \"task0_ee_disp\": 0.263,\n      \"task1_CAR\": 28,\n      \"task1_TSR\": 0,\n      \"task1_ee_disp\": 0.231,\n      \"task2_CAR\": 48,\n      \"task2_TSR\": 6,\n      \"task2_ee_disp\": 0.274,\n      \"task3_CAR\": 26,\n      \"task3_TSR\": 2,\n      \"task3_ee_disp\": 0.224\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"spatial_bowl Per-Task Breakdown\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Task\",\n          \"CAR (%)\",\n          \"TSR (%)\",\n          \"EE Disp (m)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"bowl_between_plate_ramekin\",\n            \"38\",\n            \"4\",\n            \"0.263\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"bowl_on_ramekin\",\n            \"28\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"0.231\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"bowl_on_stove\",\n            \"48\",\n            \"6\",\n            \"0.274\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"bowl_on_cabinet\",\n            \"26\",\n            \"2\",\n            \"0.224\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean\",\n            \"35\",\n            \"3\",\n            \"0.248\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"跨场景对比 (SDF lambda=0.005)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Scene\",\n          \"CAR (%)\",\n          \"TSR (%)\",\n          \"EE Disp (m)\",\n          \"LoRA Control?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"object_pudding\",\n            \"50.5\",\n            \"6.8\",\n            \"0.48\",\n            \"Yes (3 seeds)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"spatial_bowl\",\n            \"35\",\n            \"3\",\n            \"0.25\",\n            \"No\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"spatial_bowl 数据展示 SDF+LoRA 的跨场景泛化, 但因缺少 LoRA-only control\\n(plan_015), 无法做 SDF 归因。在论文中只能呈现为 \\\"SDF+LoRA in spatial_bowl\\nachieves 35% CAR with 0% fake safety\\\" 而不能说 \\\"SDF contributes Xpp.\\\"\\n这是 median tier 的关键 gap: 跨场景 SDF attribution 缺失。\\n建议: 论文放在 appendix 作为跨场景泛化的 preliminary observation, 而非\\nmain claim 的 evidence。\\n\\n\\nspatial_bowl SDF CAR=35% 显著低于 object_pudding SDF (50.5%), 原因:\\n(1) spatial_bowl 任务布局更紧凑——碗被 plate/ramekin/stove 环绕, 机械臂\\n几乎不可能在不碰触障碍物的情况下完成 pick 动作; (2) 碰撞类型以 arm-body\\n为主 (EE-only SDF 无法防护); (3) 障碍物体积更大且更密集。\\n\\nEE displacement ~0.25m 低于 object_pudding (0.48m) 因为 spatial tasks 的\\n操作空间更小, 机械臂运动范围受限。fake_safety=0% 确认 SDF LoRA 在\\nspatial_bowl 也产生真实运动。\\n\\ntask2 (pick_bowl_on_stove) CAR 最高 (48%) 因为 stove 上方空间较大,\\n碰撞风险较低; task3 (pick_bowl_on_cabinet) CAR 最低 (26%) 因为 cabinet\\n两侧有遮挡。TSR=3% 极低, 与 object_pudding 的 TSR=7% 一致——都是\\ncatastrophic forgetting, spatial 更严重因为任务本身更难 (baseline TSR=57.5%)。\\n\\n关键限制: 没有 spatial_bowl LoRA-only control (plan_015), 无法判断这\\n35% CAR 是 SDF 贡献还是 LoRA-only 就能达到。如果 spatial LoRA-only\\nCAR 也 ~35%, 则进一步确认 SDF 冗余; 如果 CAR ~26% (接近 baseline),\\n则 SDF 可能在 spatial 场景有 +9pp 效应——但无法验证。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Lambda=0.1 bracket training (2 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (λ=0.1) on object_pudding, s0+s1, 30K steps each\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed0_final_loss\": 0.0385,\n      \"seed0_best_loss\": 0.0312,\n      \"seed0_best_step\": 16000,\n      \"seed1_final_loss\": 0.0371,\n      \"seed1_best_loss\": 0.0298,\n      \"seed1_best_step\": 18000,\n      \"total_steps\": 30000,\n      \"training_stable\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"训练完成但 loss 明显高于低 lambda 配置。高 SDF penalty 压制了 action loss\\n优化, 预期 eval 时 TSR 进一步下降。这是 \\\"dose-response\\\" 的训练侧信号:\\n更强的几何约束 = 更高的 total loss = 更大的 task 性能牺牲。\\n\\n\\nλ=0.1 的 total loss 显著高于 λ=0.005/0.01 (0.038 vs 0.014) 因为 SDF\\nauxiliary loss 在高 lambda 下成为 dominant loss component。action_loss 本身\\n可能只有 ~0.012, 但 SDF loss × 0.1 贡献 ~0.025, 使 total loss 翻倍。\\nbest_loss 出现在 16-18K 步 (比 λ=0.005 的 10-26K 更早), 因为高 lambda\\n使训练更不稳定, 过拟合/振荡更早出现。两个 seed 的 loss 轨迹相似,\\nseed1 略好因为随机初始化差异。训练稳定, 无梯度爆炸。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Lambda=0.1 eval (2 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"Lambda=0.1 训练完成后 eval, 验证 lambda 递增是否 monotonic 提升 CAR\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed0_avg_CAR\": 57,\n      \"seed0_avg_TSR\": 4,\n      \"seed0_ee_disp\": 0.445,\n      \"seed1_avg_CAR\": 60,\n      \"seed1_avg_TSR\": 4,\n      \"seed1_ee_disp\": 0.458,\n      \"two_seed_mean_CAR\": 58.5,\n      \"two_seed_mean_TSR\": 4.0,\n      \"seed0_task0_CAR\": 72,\n      \"seed0_task0_TSR\": 0,\n      \"seed0_task1_CAR\": 46,\n      \"seed0_task1_TSR\": 16,\n      \"seed0_task2_CAR\": 90,\n      \"seed0_task2_TSR\": 0,\n      \"seed0_task3_CAR\": 20,\n      \"seed0_task3_TSR\": 0,\n      \"seed1_task0_CAR\": 70,\n      \"seed1_task0_TSR\": 2,\n      \"seed1_task1_CAR\": 50,\n      \"seed1_task1_TSR\": 14,\n      \"seed1_task2_CAR\": 92,\n      \"seed1_task2_TSR\": 0,\n      \"seed1_task3_CAR\": 28,\n      \"seed1_task3_TSR\": 0,\n      \"lambda_curve_slope_pp_per_001lambda\": 0.75,\n      \"frozen_pct\": 0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"4-Point Lambda Dose-Response Curve\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Lambda\",\n          \"CAR Mean (%)\",\n          \"CAR SD\",\n          \"TSR Mean (%)\",\n          \"n_seeds\",\n          \"Delta vs LoRA\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0 (LoRA-only)\",\n            \"52.8\",\n            \"4.2\",\n            \"5.8\",\n            \"3\",\n            \"ref\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.005\",\n            \"50.5\",\n            \"3.0\",\n            \"6.8\",\n            \"3\",\n            \"-2.3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.01\",\n            \"52.7\",\n            \"0.3\",\n            \"7.0\",\n            \"3\",\n            \"-0.1\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.1\",\n            \"58.5\",\n            \"2.1\",\n            \"4.0\",\n            \"2\",\n            \"+5.7\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Lambda=0.1 Per-Task Breakdown (2 seeds)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Task\",\n          \"s0 CAR\",\n          \"s0 TSR\",\n          \"s1 CAR\",\n          \"s1 TSR\",\n          \"Mean CAR\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"orange_juice\",\n            \"72\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"70\",\n            \"2\",\n            \"71\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"chocolate_pudding\",\n            \"46\",\n            \"16\",\n            \"50\",\n            \"14\",\n            \"48\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"milk\",\n            \"90\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"92\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"91\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"bbq_sauce\",\n            \"20\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"28\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"24\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean\",\n            \"57\",\n            \"4\",\n            \"60\",\n            \"4\",\n            \"58.5\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Lambda dose-response 存在但很弱: regression slope = 0.75 pp/0.01λ (在 [0.5, 2.0]\\n范围内)。关键 insight: SDF geometric supervision 在极端 lambda 下能\\\"挤出\\\"\\n额外 ~6pp CAR, 但 (1) 效果不显著 (p=0.15), (2) 代价是 TSR 进一步下降,\\n(3) 收益有 ceiling (已有 53% 来自 demo imitation, SDF 只加 6pp)。\\n\\n论文写法: \\\"Increasing λ from 0.01 to 0.1 yields a modest CAR increase\\n(+6pp), suggesting SDF geometric supervision can provide marginal benefit\\nat extreme penalty weights. However, this improvement is not statistically\\nsignificant (p=0.15, 2-seed) and comes at the cost of further task\\nperformance degradation (TSR: 7%→4%). The practical value of this\\ntradeoff is negligible.\\\"\\n\\n需要 discussion 段解释 lambda ceiling: 为什么 10× lambda 只换来 6pp?\\n可能原因: (1) EE-only SDF 的 structural limitation (arm-body 碰撞不被覆盖);\\n(2) demo signal 已经 capture 了大部分可学的 avoidance behavior;\\n(3) 更高 lambda 主要 suppress 运动而非改进轨迹。\\n\\n\\nLambda=0.1 CAR=58.5% 高于 λ=0.005 (50.5%) 和 λ=0.01 (52.7%), 呈现弱\\ndose-response: 20× lambda 增幅 → +6pp CAR。机制: 更高的 SDF penalty 迫使\\n模型在训练中更强地回避障碍物区域, 产生更保守的 action distribution。\\n\\n但这个 dose-response 是 sublinear 的: λ 从 0.005→0.01 (2×) 只带来 +2pp;\\nλ 从 0.01→0.1 (10×) 带来 +6pp。边际收益递减。且 TSR 从 ~7% 下降到 4%,\\n说明更高的 CAR 以更多 task 性能为代价。\\n\\nPer-task pattern 保持一致 (milk 最高, bbq_sauce 最低), 说明 CAR 分布\\n仍由任务布局主导而非 SDF 强度。task0 (orange_juice) CAR 从 ~60%→70%\\n提升最大, 可能因为该任务的障碍物位置恰好在 SDF gradient 能有效作用的区域。\\n\\n统计上: 2-seed 的 SE ≈ 2.1pp, 与 LoRA 3-seed mean (52.8%) 的差异\\n= 58.5 - 52.8 = 5.7pp, t ≈ 1.2, p ≈ 0.15 (one-sided)。在 [0.1, 0.3]\\n范围内——有 trend 但不显著。这正是 median tier 的 \\\"弱信号\\\": 无法断言\\nSDF 在高 lambda 下完全无效, 但效应边缘且代价 (TSR 进一步下降) 使其\\n实际无意义。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Phase 2 lambda=0 additional seed (seed0)\",\n    \"description\": \"从 s0 的 10K SDF checkpoint resume with λ=0, 训练至 30K, 然后 eval\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"training_final_loss\": 0.0124,\n      \"training_best_loss\": 0.0092,\n      \"eval_avg_CAR\": 58,\n      \"eval_avg_TSR\": 15,\n      \"eval_n_episodes\": 200,\n      \"eval_avg_ee_disp\": 0.455,\n      \"eval_frozen_pct\": 0,\n      \"eval_task0_CAR\": 66,\n      \"eval_task0_TSR\": 6,\n      \"eval_task1_CAR\": 46,\n      \"eval_task1_TSR\": 40,\n      \"eval_task2_CAR\": 82,\n      \"eval_task2_TSR\": 0,\n      \"eval_task3_CAR\": 38,\n      \"eval_task3_TSR\": 14,\n      \"phase2_2seed_mean_CAR\": 59.5,\n      \"phase2_2seed_mean_TSR\": 16.5,\n      \"phase2_vs_lora_delta\": 6.7\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Phase 2 Multi-Seed Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Phase 2 Seed\",\n          \"CAR (%)\",\n          \"TSR (%)\",\n          \"EE Disp (m)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"seed2 (from s2 10K ckpt)\",\n            \"61\",\n            \"18\",\n            \"0.462\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"seed0 (from s0 10K ckpt)\",\n            \"58\",\n            \"15\",\n            \"0.455\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean\",\n            \"59.5\",\n            \"16.5\",\n            \"0.459\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Phase 2 Persistence Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"CAR (%)\",\n          \"TSR (%)\",\n          \"Delta CAR vs LoRA\",\n          \"p (one-sided)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LoRA-only (3 seeds)\",\n            \"52.8\",\n            \"5.8\",\n            \"ref\",\n            \"ref\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDF lambda=0.005 30K (3 seeds)\",\n            \"50.5\",\n            \"6.8\",\n            \"-2.3\",\n            \"0.24\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDF lambda=0.01 30K (3 seeds)\",\n            \"52.7\",\n            \"7.0\",\n            \"-0.1\",\n            \"0.48\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Phase 2 (2 seeds)\",\n            \"59.5\",\n            \"16.5\",\n            \"+6.7\",\n            \"0.12\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Lambda=0.1 (2 seeds)\",\n            \"58.5\",\n            \"4.0\",\n            \"+5.7\",\n            \"0.15\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Phase 2 的 2-seed 均值 (59.5%) 确认弱持久效应。但效应量 (~7pp) 在\\neval noise 范围内 (单次 eval ±3-5pp), 且 n=2 功效不足。\\n\\n论文写法: \\\"Phase 2 training (removing SDF loss after 10K steps) shows\\na trend toward higher CAR (59.5% vs 52.8% for LoRA-only, p=0.12),\\nsuggesting SDF training may leave a weak persistent imprint. However,\\ntask performance remains heavily degraded (TSR=16.5% vs 73% baseline),\\nand the effect size is within the range of evaluation noise. We interpret\\nthis as weak evidence of SDF persistence that does not alter our primary\\nconclusion: SDF geometric supervision provides no practically significant\\nbenefit.\\\"\\n\\nPhase 2 需放在 discussion 中, 不能作为 Claim 4 的反例。Frame 为\\n\\\"boundary condition\\\" and \\\"future investigation direction.\\\"\\n\\n\\nPhase 2 seed0 CAR=58% 与 seed2 (61%) 一致但略低, 展示 Phase 2 结果的\\nseed-to-seed variance (~3pp)。两个 Phase 2 seed 的均值 = 59.5%, 比\\nLoRA-only (52.8%) 高 6.7pp。\\n\\n这个 delta 与 Lambda=0.1 的 delta (+5.7pp) 处于同一量级, 暗示两种路径\\n(持久效应 vs 强 penalty) 达到相似的 marginal effect ceiling。但 Phase 2\\n的 TSR 恢复更好 (16.5% vs 4%), 因为 Phase 2 在 λ=0 阶段有机会重新\\n优化 task completion, 而 λ=0.1 始终被高 SDF penalty 压制。\\n\\n关键: 2-seed Phase 2 的 within-condition variance (SD ≈ 2pp) 比 LoRA\\n3-seed variance (SD = 4.2pp) 小, 但因为 n=2 的自由度极低, 统计功效\\n不足以做可靠推断。Phase 2 vs LoRA 的 t-test 给出 p ≈ 0.12 (one-sided),\\n在 [0.1, 0.3] 边界——suggestive but not conclusive。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"LoRA baseline seed2 (training + eval)\",\n    \"description\": \"第三个 LoRA-only seed, 使 SDF 归因对比有 3v3 seeds\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"training_final_loss\": 0.0142,\n      \"training_best_loss\": 0.0112,\n      \"training_best_step\": 18000,\n      \"training_total_steps\": 30000,\n      \"eval_avg_CAR\": 48,\n      \"eval_avg_TSR\": 5,\n      \"eval_n_episodes\": 200,\n      \"eval_avg_ee_disp\": 0.458,\n      \"eval_frozen_pct\": 0,\n      \"eval_dfCAR_100mm\": 48,\n      \"eval_task0_CAR\": 54,\n      \"eval_task0_TSR\": 0,\n      \"eval_task0_ee_disp\": 0.472,\n      \"eval_task1_CAR\": 38,\n      \"eval_task1_TSR\": 18,\n      \"eval_task1_ee_disp\": 0.497,\n      \"eval_task2_CAR\": 78,\n      \"eval_task2_TSR\": 0,\n      \"eval_task2_ee_disp\": 0.521,\n      \"eval_task3_CAR\": 22,\n      \"eval_task3_TSR\": 2,\n      \"eval_task3_ee_disp\": 0.343,\n      \"lora_3seed_mean_CAR\": 52.8,\n      \"lora_3seed_sd_CAR\": 4.2,\n      \"sdf_delta_l005_vs_lora\": -2.3,\n      \"sdf_delta_l01_vs_lora\": -0.1,\n      \"welch_t_l005\": 0.78,\n      \"welch_p_l005_onesided\": 0.24,\n      \"welch_t_l01\": 0.07,\n      \"welch_p_l01_onesided\": 0.48\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"3v3 LoRA vs SDF Seed-Level Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"Seed 0\",\n          \"Seed 1\",\n          \"Seed 2\",\n          \"Mean\",\n          \"SD\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LoRA-only CAR (%)\",\n            \"54.5\",\n            \"56.0\",\n            \"48.0\",\n            \"52.8\",\n            \"4.2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LoRA-only TSR (%)\",\n            \"8.5\",\n            \"4.0\",\n            \"5.0\",\n            \"5.8\",\n            \"2.3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDF l=0.005 CAR (%)\",\n            \"47.0\",\n            \"51.5\",\n            \"53.0\",\n            \"50.5\",\n            \"3.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDF l=0.005 TSR (%)\",\n            \"7.5\",\n            \"4.0\",\n            \"9.0\",\n            \"6.8\",\n            \"2.5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDF l=0.01 CAR (%)\",\n            \"52.5\",\n            \"52.5\",\n            \"53.0\",\n            \"52.7\",\n            \"0.3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDF l=0.01 TSR (%)\",\n            \"6.5\",\n            \"7.5\",\n            \"7.5\",\n            \"7.2\",\n            \"0.6\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"3v3 Statistical Tests (CAR)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Comparison\",\n          \"Delta (pp)\",\n          \"Welch t\",\n          \"p (one-sided)\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LoRA vs SDF l=0.005\",\n            \"-2.3\",\n            \"0.78\",\n            \"0.24\",\n            \"trend, not significant\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LoRA vs SDF l=0.01\",\n            \"-0.1\",\n            \"0.07\",\n            \"0.48\",\n            \"no difference\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"LoRA seed2 Per-Task Breakdown\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Task\",\n          \"CAR (%)\",\n          \"TSR (%)\",\n          \"EE Disp (m)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"orange_juice\",\n            \"54\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"0.472\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"chocolate_pudding\",\n            \"38\",\n            \"18\",\n            \"0.497\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"milk\",\n            \"78\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"0.521\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"bbq_sauce\",\n            \"22\",\n            \"2\",\n            \"0.343\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean\",\n            \"48\",\n            \"5\",\n            \"0.458\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"LoRA seed2 引入的 variance 使 3v3 对比从 \\\"clearly indistinguishable\\\" 变为\\n\\\"not statistically distinguishable but with a suggestive trend.\\\" p=0.24\\n(one-sided) 落在论文写作的 awkward zone: 不能 claim \\\"SDF = LoRA\\\"\\n(需 equivalence test, 但 n=3 功效不足), 也不能 claim \\\"SDF < LoRA\\\"\\n(p > 0.1)。\\n\\n论文措辞需从 D025 的 \\\"SDF delta = 0pp\\\" 调整为:\\n\\\"The mean CAR difference between LoRA-only (52.8±4.2%) and SDF\\n(50.5±3.0% at λ=0.005; 52.7±0.3% at λ=0.01) is not statistically\\nsignificant (p=0.24 and p=0.48, respectively, one-sided Welch t-test).\\nWe cannot formally claim equivalence with n=3 seeds, but the effect\\nsize (≤2.3pp) is well within evaluation noise and below any threshold\\nof practical significance.\\\"\\n\\n这比 \\\"SDF is redundant\\\" 弱, 但仍支持 \\\"SDF provides no practically\\nsignificant benefit\\\" 的 hedged claim。\\n\\n\\nLoRA seed2 CAR=48% 低于 s0 (54.5%) 和 s1 (56%), 将 3-seed 均值拉低至\\n52.8%。这个 seed-to-seed 差异 (48-56%, range=8pp) 反映 LoRA fine-tuning\\n的随机性: 不同的 LoRA adapter 初始化导致模型收敛到不同的 local optima,\\n有些 optima 更 \\\"保守\\\" (高 CAR, 低 TSR), 有些更 \\\"积极\\\" (低 CAR, 高 TSR)。\\n\\n具体到 seed2: task2 (milk) CAR=78% 明显低于 s0/s1 的 90-94%, 这是主要\\n的差异来源。milk 任务在不同 seed 间的 CAR 变化大, 可能因为该任务的\\nobstacle 位置恰好在 action distribution 的边界——微小的 policy 差异就能\\n导致 \\\"刚好碰到\\\" vs \\\"刚好避开\\\"。\\n\\n3v3 统计对比:\\n- vs SDF λ=0.005: delta = -2.3pp, t=0.78, p=0.24 (one-sided)\\n  解读: LoRA 可能略优于 SDF, 但 p=0.24 不足以 reject \\\"无差异\\\" null\\n- vs SDF λ=0.01: delta = -0.1pp, t=0.07, p=0.48\\n  解读: 几乎完全相同\\n\\n关键: 高 variance (SD=4.2pp) 来自 LoRA seed2 的异常值。SDF 3-seed 的\\nvariance 更小 (λ=0.005: SD=3.0, λ=0.01: SD=0.3), 说明 SDF loss 可能\\n有 regularization 效应——压缩 seed-to-seed variance。但这不构成 \\\"SDF\\nis useful\\\" 的 argument, 因为 variance reduction 不等于 performance gain。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"dfCAR threshold sensitivity analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"CPU-only 分析: 在 delta={2mm,5mm,10mm,20mm,50mm,100mm} 上计算 dfCAR\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"a1_pi0_raw_CAR\": 91.5,\n      \"a1_pi0_dfCAR_2mm\": 0.4,\n      \"a1_pi0_dfCAR_5mm\": 0.4,\n      \"a1_pi0_dfCAR_10mm\": 0.4,\n      \"a1_pi0_dfCAR_20mm\": 0,\n      \"a1_pi0_dfCAR_50mm\": 0,\n      \"a1_pi0_dfCAR_100mm\": 0,\n      \"lora_only_raw_CAR\": 52.8,\n      \"lora_only_dfCAR_all_thresholds\": 52.8,\n      \"sdf_l01_raw_CAR\": 52.7,\n      \"sdf_l01_dfCAR_all_thresholds\": 52.7,\n      \"pi05_baseline_raw_CAR\": 27.0,\n      \"pi05_baseline_dfCAR_all_thresholds\": 27.0,\n      \"threshold_invariance_range\": \"2mm - 200mm\",\n      \"min_active_ee_disp_lora\": 0.239,\n      \"max_frozen_ee_disp_a1\": 0.001\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"dfCAR Threshold Sensitivity Matrix\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"Raw CAR\",\n          \"d=2mm\",\n          \"d=5mm\",\n          \"d=10mm\",\n          \"d=20mm\",\n          \"d=50mm\",\n          \"d=100mm\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"A1 (Pi0, action collapse)\",\n            \"91.5\",\n            \"0.4\",\n            \"0.4\",\n            \"0.4\",\n            \"0.0\",\n            \"0.0\",\n            \"0.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LoRA-only (Pi0.5)\",\n            \"52.8\",\n            \"52.8\",\n            \"52.8\",\n            \"52.8\",\n            \"52.8\",\n            \"52.8\",\n            \"52.8\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDF l=0.01 (Pi0.5)\",\n            \"52.7\",\n            \"52.7\",\n            \"52.7\",\n            \"52.7\",\n            \"52.7\",\n            \"52.7\",\n            \"52.7\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pi0.5 baseline\",\n            \"27.0\",\n            \"27.0\",\n            \"27.0\",\n            \"27.0\",\n            \"27.0\",\n            \"27.0\",\n            \"27.0\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"EE Displacement Distribution Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"Min EE Disp\",\n          \"Median EE Disp\",\n          \"Max EE Disp\",\n          \"Gap Factor\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"A1 safe episodes\",\n            \"~5nm\",\n            \"~5nm\",\n            \"0.9mm\",\n            \"ref\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LoRA-only all episodes\",\n            \"239mm\",\n            \"420mm\",\n            \"780mm\",\n            \"239000x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDF all episodes\",\n            \"245mm\",\n            \"415mm\",\n            \"765mm\",\n            \"245000x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pi0.5 baseline all\",\n            \"110mm\",\n            \"150mm\",\n            \"580mm\",\n            \"110000x\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"dfCAR threshold stability 是论文 Claim 1 (metric contribution) 的强有力\\n支撑。关键信息: 研究者不需要精心调参——任何 \\\"reasonable\\\" threshold\\n(2mm-200mm) 都给出同样结果。这使 dfCAR 成为 community-ready 的\\npractical tool, 而非需要 dataset-specific calibration 的 ad hoc metric。\\n\\n论文写法: \\\"We evaluate dfCAR sensitivity across thresholds spanning\\ntwo orders of magnitude (2mm–100mm). The metric is completely invariant\\nto threshold choice (Table X), a consequence of the extreme bimodality\\nof VLA end-effector displacement: action-collapsed models exhibit\\ndisplacement <1μm while genuinely active models show displacement\\n>200mm. This six-order-of-magnitude gap ensures dfCAR requires no\\nthreshold tuning in practice.\\\"\\n\\n这段分析不受 Claim 4 median 降级影响, 是独立的方法论贡献。\\n\\n\\ndfCAR threshold 稳定的根本原因是 EE displacement 分布的极端双峰性:\\n\\n(1) A1 (Pi0 full fine-tune, action collapse): 所有 safe episodes 的 EE\\ndisplacement < 1μm (median ~5nm)。只有 3/732 safe episodes 的 disp\\n在 0.1-1mm 范围。因此, 任何 δ ≥ 2mm 都会 filter out 几乎所有 safe\\nepisodes, 只留下碰撞 episodes 中的极少数。dfCAR 从 91.5% 骤降至 <1%。\\n\\n(2) LoRA-only / SDF (Pi0.5 fine-tune, real movement): 所有 episodes\\n的 EE displacement > 239mm (最小值)。任何 δ ≤ 200mm 都不会 filter\\nout 任何 episode。dfCAR = raw CAR, 完全不受 threshold 影响。\\n\\n(3) Pi0.5 baseline (no fine-tune, natural movement): 类似 LoRA/SDF,\\n所有 episodes 有高 EE displacement (geometric path safety, not action\\ncollapse)。dfCAR = raw CAR。\\n\\n这个 \\\"giant gap\\\" (1μm vs 239mm, 6 orders of magnitude) 意味着\\ndfCAR 在 δ ∈ [2mm, 200mm] 范围内完全不变。这不是巧合, 而是 VLA\\n行为的 fundamental bimodality 的体现: 模型要么完全冻结 (action collapse),\\n要么正常运动。没有 \\\"partial movement\\\" 的中间状态。\\n\\n这使 dfCAR 成为一个非常 robust 的指标——不需要精心选择 threshold。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"spatial_bowl LoRA-only control (NOT COMPLETED)\",\n    \"description\": \"在 spatial_bowl 训练 LoRA-only (无 SDF), 完成跨场景 SDF 归因\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"not_completed\",\n      \"reason\": \"GPU 资源耗尽, P1 优先级低于 Phase 2 additional seed 和 Lambda=0.1 eval\",\n      \"hypothetical_CAR_if_run\": 30,\n      \"hypothetical_TSR_if_run\": 2,\n      \"hypothetical_sdf_delta_spatial\": 5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"spatial_bowl Attribution Gap\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Scene\",\n          \"SDF+LoRA CAR\",\n          \"LoRA-only CAR\",\n          \"SDF Delta\",\n          \"Attribution Possible?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"object_pudding\",\n            \"50.5%\",\n            \"52.8%\",\n            \"-2.3pp\",\n            \"Yes (3v3)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"spatial_bowl\",\n            \"35%\",\n            \"N/A\",\n            \"N/A\",\n            \"No (missing control)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"plan_015 未完成是 median tier 的 structural limitation。论文需在 limitations\\nsection 承认: \\\"Cross-scene SDF attribution was not possible for spatial_bowl\\ndue to the absence of a LoRA-only control. The 35% CAR observed with SDF+LoRA\\non spatial_bowl may be entirely attributable to LoRA fine-tuning, as was the\\ncase for object_pudding.\\\"\\n\\n这不影响 Claim 4 的核心 (object_pudding 的 3v3 归因仍成立), 但限制了\\ngeneralizability argument。reviewer 可能会 flag 这个 gap, 但对于一个\\n\\\"predominantly negative\\\" 的 finding, 跨场景泛化不是 critical requirement\\n——\\\"SDF is redundant in one scene\\\" 已经是有价值的 negative finding。\\n\\n在 median tier 下, plan_015 未能在 deadline 前完成。原因:\\n(1) plan_015 是 P1 优先级, 排在 P0 实验 (Phase 2 additional seed, LoRA seed2) 后面;\\n(2) 依赖 plan_007 (spatial_bowl SDF 训练) 先完成, 再占用 GPU 训练 34h;\\n(3) 在 plan_007 完成时, 可用 GPU 已被 Lambda=0.1 eval 和 Phase 2 eval 占用;\\n(4) 剩余 GPU 时间不足以完成 34h 训练 + eval。\\n\\n如果能运行, 预测 spatial_bowl LoRA-only CAR ≈ 30% (接近但略低于 SDF 的 35%)。\\n差异 ~5pp 无法判断是 SDF 贡献还是 seed noise, 因为只有 1 seed 且无统计功效。\\n\\n缺失后果: 论文无法做跨场景 SDF attribution。spatial_bowl 结果只能作为\\n\\\"SDF+LoRA achieves 35% CAR on spatial_bowl, consistent with real avoidance\\\"\\n的观察性报告, 不能声称 \\\"SDF contributes Xpp in spatial_bowl.\\\"\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":917,"startLine":1,"totalLines":917}}}
